  #line-at(96pt, 124.56pt, "The industrial standard ASTM D5470 [9] remains the most widely used method for TIM ")
  #line-at(72pt, 145.44pt, "evaluation. However, as a steady-state one-dimensional method, it primarily yields an overall ")
  #line-at(72pt, 166.08pt, "thermal resistance and does not determine the volumetric heat capacity. Moreover, separating ")
  #line-at(72pt, 186.72pt, "intrinsic thermal conductivity from interfacial thermal resistance usually requires ")
  #line-at(72pt, 207.36pt, "measurements at multiple bond-line thicknesses, which implicitly assumes that the TIM ")
  #line-at(72pt, 228.24pt, "microstructure remains unchanged across the tested samples. This assumption becomes ")
  #line-at(72pt, 248.88pt, "questionable for highly compliant TIMs, especially gels and greases that may undergo squeeze ")
  #line-at(72pt, 269.52pt, "flow, phase redistribution, or pressure-induced structural rearrangement. ")
  #line-at(96pt, 290.16pt, "Transient macroscopic techniques such as laser flash analysis (LFA) can determine ")
  #line-at(72pt, 311.04pt, "thermal diffusivity, i.e., ")
