#original-page(595pt, 842pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(294.725pt, 804.24pt, "4 ")
  #line-at(96pt, 83.28pt, "The square-pulsed source (SPS) thermoreflectance technique provides an opportunity to ")
  #line-at(72pt, 103.92pt, "address this problem. In SPS, the pump beam is modulated by a 50% duty-cycle square wave ")
  #line-at(72pt, 124.56pt, "over an exceptionally broad frequency window from 1 Hz to 10 MHz [15, 18], and the time-")
  #line-at(72pt, 145.44pt, "resolved thermoreflectance response is interpreted with a heat-transfer model. This broad range ")
  #line-at(72pt, 166.08pt, "allows the thermal penetration depth to vary over several orders of magnitude, thereby ")
  #line-at(72pt, 186.72pt, "providing access to distinct timescales of heat storage, heat diffusion, and interfacial heat ")
  #line-at(72pt, 207.36pt, "transfer within a single experimental framework. SPS has previously been shown to ")
  #line-at(72pt, 228.24pt, "simultaneously determine thermal conductivity and volumetric heat capacity across diverse ")
  #line-at(72pt, 248.88pt, "materials [15, 19], and it has also been extended to multilayer structures and convective heat-")
  #line-at(72pt, 269.52pt, "transfer measurements [18, 20]. However, its capability for pressure-controlled TIM ")
  #line-at(72pt, 290.16pt, "assemblies, where bulk and interfacial properties evolve together, has not yet been ")
  #line-at(72pt, 311.04pt, "demonstrated. ")
  #line-at(96pt, 331.68pt, "Against this background, the present study addresses three knowledge gaps: the lack of a ")
  #line-at(72pt, 352.32pt, "single transient method that simultaneously resolves ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(334.815pt, 352.32pt, "k")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(340.141pt, 352.32pt, ", ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(347.617pt, 352.32pt, "C")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(355.621pt, 352.32pt, ", and ITR in TIM assemblies; the ")
  #line-at(72pt, 372.96pt, "limited understanding of how these parameters evolve with pressure and loading history; and ")
  #line-at(72pt, 393.84pt, "the insufficient linkage between TIM property characterization and the thermal processes that ")
  #line-at(72pt, 414.48pt, "govern electronic packaging performance. To address these gaps, we combine SPS ")
  #line-at(72pt, 435.12pt, "thermoreflectance with a pressure-controlled sample platform and examine three representative ")
  #line-at(72pt, 455.76pt, "TIM classes: a thermally conductive gel, a thermal pad, and a high-vacuum grease. Section 2 ")
  #line-at(72pt, 476.64pt, "describes the SPS principle, the pressure-controlled measurement configuration, the tested ")
  #line-at(72pt, 497.28pt, "materials, and the uncertainty framework. Section 3 then presents representative signal ")
  #line-at(72pt, 517.92pt, "decoupling and the pressure-dependent thermal behavior of the three TIMs, followed by ")
  #line-at(72pt, 538.56pt, "physics-based interpretation of their bulk-state and interfacial evolution. By doing so, this work ")
