#original-page(595pt, 842pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(291.725pt, 804.24pt, "15 ")
  #line-at(72pt, 83.28pt, "interfacial conformity rather than to changes in bulk transport. The fitted curve captures the ")
  #line-at(72pt, 103.92pt, "experimental data well, confirming that the main role of pressure in this material is to improve ")
  #line-at(72pt, 124.56pt, "the interface. ")
  #line-at(96pt, 145.44pt, "These observations have an important physical implication. For grease-type TIMs, the ")
  #line-at(72pt, 166.08pt, "bulk material behaves approximately as an invariant thermal medium under the present loading ")
  #line-at(72pt, 186.72pt, "conditions, whereas the interface remains highly pressure-sensitive. In other words, the thermal ")
  #line-at(72pt, 207.36pt, "response is governed predominantly by how effectively the grease wets and bridges the ")
  #line-at(72pt, 228.24pt, "contacting solids, rather than by compression-induced changes in its intrinsic bulk state. This ")
  #line-at(72pt, 248.88pt, "behavior is consistent with the intended function of greases as highly conformable interstitial ")
  #line-at(72pt, 269.52pt, "fillers. ")
  #line-at(96pt, 290.16pt, "Taken together, the results in Fig. 5 complement those of Figs. 3 and 4 by showing that ")
  #line-at(72pt, 311.04pt, "different classes of TIMs respond to pressure through fundamentally different mechanisms. ")
  #line-at(72pt, 331.68pt, "Whereas gels and pads exhibit coupled bulk-state and interface evolution, grease responds ")
  #line-at(72pt, 352.32pt, "mainly through interface evolution. This contrast underscores the importance of separating ")
  #line-at(72pt, 372.96pt, "bulk and interfacial contributions when evaluating TIMs under realistic assembly conditions. ")
  #line-at(72pt, 393.84pt, "It also indicates that, for grease-based interfaces, engineering optimization should focus ")
  #line-at(72pt, 414.48pt, "primarily on wetting, spreading, and contact formation, while for gels and pads both bulk-state ")
  #line-at(72pt, 435.12pt, "evolution and contact evolution must be considered. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72pt, 476.64pt, "4. CONCLUSIONS  ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(96pt, 497.28pt, "This work presents a square-pulsed source (SPS) thermoreflectance method for the ")
  #line-at(72pt, 517.92pt, "simultaneous measurement of thermal conductivity, volumetric heat capacity, and interfacial ")
  #line-at(72pt, 538.56pt, "thermal resistance in thermal interface material assemblies under compressive loading. The ")
  #line-at(72pt, 559.44pt, "originality of the study lies in resolving, within a single transient measurement framework, the ")
  #line-at(72pt, 580.08pt, "path-dependent evolution of both bulk and interfacial thermal properties under realistic ")
  #line-at(72pt, 600.72pt, "assembly conditions. By combining a broad modulation-frequency range with time-resolved ")
  #line-at(72pt, 621.36pt, "thermoreflectance detection and inverse analysis, the method separates heat storage, heat ")
  #line-at(72pt, 642.24pt, "diffusion, and interfacial heat transfer without requiring the heat capacity to be prescribed a ")
  #line-at(72pt, 662.88pt, "priori. ")
  #line-at(96pt, 683.52pt, "Measurements on a thermally conductive gel, a thermal pad, and a high-vacuum grease ")
  #line-at(72pt, 704.16pt, "reveal distinct pressure-dependent thermal processes. For the gel and pad, both bulk properties ")
  #line-at(72pt, 725.04pt, "and interfacial thermal resistance evolve significantly with pressure and show clear loading-")
  #line-at(72pt, 745.68pt, "unloading hysteresis, indicating persistent changes in bulk state and interfacial conformity. For ")
  #line-at(72pt, 766.32pt, "the grease, in contrast, the bulk thermal conductivity and volumetric heat capacity remain ")
]

